{
  "finding": "Scenes S009, S010, and S011 depict a vessel fire ignited by a flare gun, fireworks mortars overhead, and a performer diving into cold harbor water at night near an adjacent skiff with a child character and dog. If practical pyrotechnic special effects are staged, Industry-Wide Safety Bulletin #16 requires that any required licenses and permits be obtained from the proper Authorities Having Jurisdiction (AHJ) prior to use, and that pyrotechnic special effects operators hold valid applicable licenses. Additionally, Safety Bulletin #17 specifies that water temperature and exposure be monitored and that production management take steps to prevent hypothermia during cast and crew water operations. Staging execution (practical open-water burn vs. controlled tank or VFX) and actual performer casting/doubling remain unconfirmed production facts.",
  "remedy_detail": "If practical pyrotechnics or open flames are utilized, engage a licensed Pyrotechnic Special Effects Operator holding valid state/federal licenses and obtain required permits from the proper Authorities Having Jurisdiction prior to shooting. For water immersion scenes, implement protocols to monitor temperature and take necessary steps to prevent hypothermia among cast and crew. Confirm whether the sequence will be executed practically, in a controlled tank facility, or augmented via visual effects, and confirm casting and stunt doubling arrangements.",
  "remedy_action": "ADD_SPECIALIST",
  "severity": "HIGH"
}

